{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_65","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1748,1783p' src/cljc/yang/python/antlr/lower.cljc; tail -10 collab/p5b-jvm-slow.log; tail -10 collab/p5b-node-targeted.log; rg -n 'defn.*publish|verify' src/cljc/yin/vm/linker/publish.cljc | head -20\"","aggregated_output":"(defn lower-packet\n  \"The complete program for one ok packet: the module body run by\n   `py/run-main`, with tail calls marked. Its value is `{:py/out [...]\n   :py/exception nil-or-{:type :args}}`. The packet may declare the\n   decimal digit budget of its literals as `:yang.python.antlr/max-digits`.\n\n   `:prelude` selects how the runtime profile arrives: `:bundled` (the\n   default) carries the prelude tree ahead of the body; `:linked`\n   requires the module `py` from the task's link pair, then allocates the\n   task's runtime state with `(py/init!)`. Either way the body names only\n   `py/` exports, never a runtime key.\n\n   A unit that statically imports a module needs it delivered: under\n   `:linked` one `(require 'pym.<name>)` per import is hoisted after the\n   `py` require (ruling 4's explicit eager-dependency restriction; an\n   import-free unit's tree is unchanged). Imports need the linked\n   prelude -- a module closure's free reads never see the ambient store,\n   so a bundled importer's `py/*` definitions are invisible to an\n   imported body -- and a bundled unit holding an import is refused.\"\n  ([packet] (lower-packet packet {}))\n  ([packet {:keys [prelude], :or {prelude :bundled}}]\n   (let [requires (import-requires (p/validate! packet))\n         main (app* 'py/run-main\n                    (u/lam [globals-sym globals-fn-sym]\n                           (lower-module-body packet)))]\n     (u/mark-tails\n       (case prelude\n         :bundled (if (seq requires)\n                    (throw (ex-info\n                             \"Imports need the linked prelude (docs/design/yang.antlr.md 8.5.6)\"\n                             {:yang.python.antlr/diagnostic :yang.python.antlr/unsupported,\n                              :construct \"import under the bundled prelude\"}))\n                    (u/then prelude/uast main))\n         :linked (u/seq-nodes\n                   (into [(app* 'require (u/lit prelude/module-name))]\n                         (concat (mapv #(app* 'require (u/lit %)) requires)\nLoading initial Timbre config from: :default\n\nRunning tests in #{\"test\"}\nWARNING: load already refers to: #'clojure.core/load in namespace: yin.vm.encoder, being replaced by: #'yin.vm.encoder/load\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test\nTesting yin.vm.debruijn.stack-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.parity-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic-register.code-test\n\nTesting yin.vm.semantic-register.derive-test\nC4 preparing published py module\n95:   own content, `:verifying` with discharge deferred, as a serving\n110:             :derivation :verifying\n115:(defn- publish-closure!\n210:(defn publish-module!\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
