ered FROM A alone, never from the tree and never through the old lowerers. No adapter. No version bump. R and H need NOT equal the old bytes or each other; the old compilers are an EXECUTION oracle only.\\012- A is the only code identity; new identities use Jing's default digest (BLAKE3). The only SHA-256 use is the existing descriptor-hash function.\\012- Do not change the design: on an ambiguity or conflict record it in the report with the evidence and the smallest reading you took.\\012- Verify every hand-derived number (the design marks them) on the FIRST run; report a wrong one plainly, never adjust silently.\\012\\012## Rules\\012\\012- **Tests that can fail.** Before reporting, for each behaviour you consider hardest (at least eight for this slice), apply a mutation to the source temporarily, confirm a NAMED test fails, and restore the file byte for byte (take a verified backup FIRST into `/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p5b/collab/`, and restore from it; check with `git diff --quiet HEAD -- <path>`). Put the table in the report. A surviving mutant is a finding.\\012- Portability traps (Dart/Node): use `#?(:cljd nil :clj ...)` with `:cljd` FIRST; no private-var access across namespaces; `(- x)` on a float; `for` over a >32-element seq (use keep/mapv); `(assoc nil :a 1 :b 2)` (start from `{}`); protocol methods need distinct param names; cljd EDN reader whitespace before closers; maps may carry nil-valued keys.\\012- **zsh does not word-split an unquoted variable.** Never put a namespace list in a variable; write each `-n namespace` literally.\\012- Foreground only; never `&`; never background a lane.\\012- Sandbox honesty: if a command cannot run in your sandbox (the Dart lane), record the exact command and error and say that lane was NOT RUN. The orchestrator re-runs every lane.\\012- Do NOT `git add` or `git commit`; do not stage `collab/`.\\012\\012## Scope\\012\\012Exactly the slice named in design §10.2 (slice 5b; items 1-11): its files to create/ch